{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/11/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/11`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/11/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n- `description`：在一个包含多个同心矩形框的网格中，每层框的颜色编码了一个\"传播指令\"——从最内层向外逐层读取指令，将核心图案按指令序列依次变换后输出。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中心有一个小型多色图案（核心精灵，如 3×3）。\n  - 核心精灵外围是若干层同心单像素宽矩形框，从内到外依次编号为第1层、第2层……\n  - 每层框使用以下四种颜色之一：Red 表示\"水平翻转\"，Blue 表示\"垂直翻转\"，Green 表示\"顺时针旋转90°\"，Yellow 表示\"逆时针旋转90°\"。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从最内层框开始，向外逐层读取每层框的颜色，构成一个变换指令序列。\n  - 对核心精灵依次执行该指令序列中的每个变换操作。\n  - 输出仅包含最终变换后的核心精灵（紧贴边界框输出，无多余背景）。\n- `Key insight`：同心框不是装饰边界，而是一个从内向外排列的指令队列；解题者必须先发现颜色到变换操作的映射关系，再按正确的层序（由内向外）依次应用，才能得到正确输出。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/afe3afe9, train/34cfa167, eval/291dc1e1, train/2601afb7, train/b25e450b, eval/fc7cae8d, eval/88e364bc, train/4df5b0ae\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"afe3afe9\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3688\nmechanism=0.4665\nlexical=0.0181\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/afe3afe9.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/afe3afe9.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConvert each hollow 3x3 symbol to one pixel and slide the pixels clockwise from the marked edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a background, one full-edge marker line, and monochrome hollow 3x3 foreground symbols.\n- The symbols lie on a coarse row/column lattice; fully empty lattice rows or columns are absent from the output.\n\nRule\n- Replace each hollow 3x3 symbol with one pixel of its color in the corresponding coarse-grid cell.\n- The marker edge gives the compaction direction by clockwise border travel: top -> right, right -> down, bottom -> left, left -> up.\n- Preserve the order of non-background pixels while sliding them as far as possible in that direction.\n\nKey insight\n- The large picture is a scaled symbolic grid, and the blue edge marker acts as a gravity direction rather than as output content.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow 3x3 foreground symbols collapsed to one coarse-grid pixel each; the full-edge blue marker selects the path direction\",\n  \"path\": \"straight along each coarse row or column in clockwise border direction from the marker edge: top->right, right->down, bottom->left, left->up; stop when packed against the boundary or previous pixel\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"stably compact all non-background coarse pixels in each parallel line, preserving their order\",\n  \"transform\": \"discard the blue marker and fully empty coarse rows or columns; replace each hollow 3x3 symbol by its color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"occupied coarse lattice after empty rows or columns are dropped\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3251\nmechanism=0.4028\nlexical=0.0159\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/34cfa167.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"291dc1e1\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3402\nmechanism=0.4041\nlexical=0.0269\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/291dc1e1.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/291dc1e1.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.\n- \"Blue\" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is \"red.\"\n- Solid rectangles in the interior.\n\nRule:\n- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).\n- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.\n\nKey insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"rectangles\",\n  \"dst\": \"into slot center aligned\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"(distance(s, blue_edge), distance(s, red_edge)).order == d.pos.row.order\",\n  \"transform\": \"rot90 if blue edge is vertical\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"move rectangles in order, one below another\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2601afb7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3071\nmechanism=0.3406\nlexical=0.0175\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2601afb7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2601afb7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate each vertical bar's color one slot right and its height one slot left.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background surrounds several monochrome one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Every bar is bottom-aligned and occupies a distinct column.\n- The ordered bar slots are read from left to right.\n\nRule\n- Keep the grid shape and the bar columns unchanged.\n- At slot i, use the color from the previous slot cyclically