ular mask s touching exactly one outer border\",\n  \"path\": \"straight slide from s to the opposite border along its row band or column band, determined by the touched border\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"recolor the complete swept row/column stripe orange, then place s at the opposite edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"all black masks move simultaneously; destination black masks overwrite orange trails and any grey cells, while cells outside swept stripes remain unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"fc7cae8d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2975\nmechanism=0.3568\nlexical=0.0175\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/fc7cae8d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/fc7cae8d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAlign a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).\n- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.\n- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.\n\nKey insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
